{"name":"Goblin","hex":"#34533d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goblin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Traditionally, a supernatural being of folklore, typically small and grotesque or misshapen, that commonly haunts dark places, often mischievous or malevolent; a type of evil elf, sprite, or demon.","In later fantasy literature, an evil and grotesquely ugly humanoid, typically powerful and warlike, often associated with orcs and trolls."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goblin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goblin","blocks":[{"text":"A goblin is a diminutive, grotesque, and often malevolent humanoid creature prominent in European folklore, typically characterized by its mischievous or demonic nature, small stature, furry or leathery appearance, and ability to shapeshift. Goblins are believed to dwell in subterranean areas or households, where they engage in acts ranging from pranks to murder. Their etymology derives from Old French gobelin, possibly linked to Medieval Latin gobelinus or Greek kobalos, though some scholars trace it to earlier domestic protector spirits like the Germanic kobold, which were later demonized under Christian influence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Goblin_illustration_from_19th_century.png/330px-Goblin_illustration_from_19th_century.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblin","wikidata":"Q308697"},{"title":"Goblin (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Goblin is an Italian progressive rock band known for their film scores. They frequently collaborate with Dario Argento, most notably creating the scores for Profondo Rosso in 1975 and Suspiria in 1977. Because their collaborator Dario Argento specializes in creating horror, suspense and slasher/giallo genre movies, scores made by Goblin in these movies often had eerie and ominous tones. CD re-releases of their scores have performed well, especially in Germany and Japan. Goblin returned with a series of live concerts in Europe in 2009 and in North America in 2013."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Goblin_%28band%29.jpg/330px-Goblin_%28band%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblin_(band)","wikidata":"Q1317474"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/The_princess_and_the_goblin_%281920%29_%2814566641580%29.jpg/500px-The_princess_and_the_goblin_%281920%29_%2814566641580%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/The_princess_and_the_goblin_%281920%29_%2814566641580%29.jpg/1280px-The_princess_and_the_goblin_%281920%29_%2814566641580%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/The_princess_and_the_goblin_%281920%29_%2814566641580%29.jpg/500px-The_princess_and_the_goblin_%281920%29_%2814566641580%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Princess and the Goblin by George MacDonald, illustrated by Jessie Willcox Smith, 1920","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_princess_and_the_goblin_(1920)_(14566641580).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/DnD_Goblin.png/500px-DnD_Goblin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/DnD_Goblin.png/500px-DnD_Goblin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Representation of a goblin as it appears in the fantasy role-playing game Dungeons & Dragons","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADnD_Goblin.png"}],"sounds":{"goblin":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/w